WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:01.453
- Hi guys, it's Inga.

00:00:15.202 --> 00:00:17.785
(upbeat music)

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:20.577
- Hi, I'm Adrienne Borlongan,

00:00:20.577 --> 00:00:23.280
I'm on of the co-founders
of Wanderlust Creamery.

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:24.810
We're an artisanal ice cream shop,

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:26.200
we make everything in house

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:28.470
and all of our flavors
are inspired by travel.

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:31.040
Today we're having Inga
coming to make some ice cream,

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:32.280
it's gonna be really fun.

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:34.830
- I'm finally here, I
wanted to do something today

00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:36.620
that kind of represents my background.

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:39.360
I'm half Taiwanese and I'm
half Hong Kong Chinese.

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:40.810
- All the best desserts come from there.

00:00:40.810 --> 00:00:43.640
- Yes, Hong Kong egg tarts are so popular.

00:00:43.640 --> 00:00:46.100
- That custard flavor, put in some shards

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:47.500
of flaky, caramelized puff pastry.

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:49.470
- Oh my god, sounds so good.

00:00:49.470 --> 00:00:51.750
Oolong tea is super big in Taiwan.

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:54.040
Mom would always buy pineapple pastries.

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:56.920
- Maybe we can do an
oolong infused ice cream

00:00:56.920 --> 00:00:59.420
with some pineapple
pastry pieces in there.

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:00.253
- Let's do it!

00:01:01.224 --> 00:01:02.940
(pleasant music)

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:04.100
- We're gonna start with our base.

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:08.100
Organic grass fed dairy,
eggs, a little bit of sugar.

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:10.760
For this one, we're using 16% butter fat

00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:12.430
because we want it a little richer.

00:01:12.430 --> 00:01:13.763
- This looks super creamy.

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:16.320
- We're gonna add some Taiwanese oolong.

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:18.160
I picked this variety because it's known

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:20.960
for having like a really
buttery, milky flavor.

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:21.793
- I love that.

00:01:21.793 --> 00:01:24.293
- We're just gonna heat
that until it infuses.

00:01:24.590 --> 00:01:26.173
- Look at this, swirly.

00:01:26.830 --> 00:01:28.610
- [Adrienne] Basically bringing the base

00:01:28.610 --> 00:01:30.323
to just a low simmer.

00:01:30.550 --> 00:01:34.350
- Oh, you can actually
smell it, this is so cool.

00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:36.260
- And now we're gonna
take this and strain it.

00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:37.283
- Y'all ready?

00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:41.770
Oh my god, you can actually see

00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:44.363
this many tea leaves in there, I love it.

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:45.953
We did it.

00:01:45.953 --> 00:01:47.800
- Press down really hard on that.

00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:50.480
- You squeeze it all
out, is it coming out?

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:51.313
Oh my god.

00:01:52.932 --> 00:01:53.765
Okay.

00:01:53.950 --> 00:01:55.800
- Do you wanna taste your concoction?

00:01:57.057 --> 00:02:00.830
- Oh, it tastes like
really creamy boba tea

00:02:00.830 --> 00:02:02.820
and it's not bitter, this is so good.

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:04.060
I would just eat it like this.

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:06.050
- We're gonna cut up our pineapple pastry.

00:02:06.050 --> 00:02:07.750
- [Inga] Sheer pineapple goodness.

00:02:08.671 --> 00:02:10.790
(pleasant music)

00:02:10.790 --> 00:02:13.100
- Now that we have the
oolong tea already done,

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:14.690
we're gonna set that one aside

00:02:14.710 --> 00:02:17.663
and we're gonna start with our
Hong Kong egg tart ice cream.

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:20.373
We're gonna separate some egg yolks.

00:02:21.271 --> 00:02:23.970
(metallic clanking)

00:02:23.970 --> 00:02:25.817
- Okay, there we go, egg whites in here.

00:02:25.817 --> 00:02:26.650
- [Adrienne] Yes.

00:02:26.650 --> 00:02:28.840
- Wow, I am really bad at this today.

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:29.673
Yes!

00:02:30.666 --> 00:02:31.499
- Oh.

00:02:32.155 --> 00:02:32.988
- Oh sorry, sorry, sorry, sorry.

00:02:32.988 --> 00:02:33.946
- It's okay.

00:02:33.946 --> 00:02:36.196
(laughing)

00:02:36.424 --> 00:02:37.257
- I'm sorry!

00:02:37.257 --> 00:02:39.080
- I have a spoon, don't worry.

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:41.173
- I did it, beautiful.

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:43.480
- We're adding our base again,

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:45.760
we're adding extra egg
yolks to make it really.

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:46.593
- Extra yolk-y.

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:48.793
- Let's heat this baby up, break it up.

00:02:50.210 --> 00:02:51.770
This is pretty much warm.

00:02:51.770 --> 00:02:53.903
You're just gonna put a little splash.

00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:55.653
- Beautiful color.

00:02:55.700 --> 00:02:57.750
- And then you're gonna add that to this.

00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:00.900
Does that smell familiar to you?

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:02.063
- That does!

00:03:03.770 --> 00:03:05.850
- To give it more egg flavor,

00:03:05.850 --> 00:03:09.133
we're using this Indian
ingredient called black salt.

00:03:09.150 --> 00:03:11.253
- This is labeled egg farts.

00:03:11.510 --> 00:03:13.320
- It's literally labeled egg farts

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:15.420
because it smells like egg fart, smell it.

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:18.720
- Okay, yeah, it does smell like it.

00:03:19.210 --> 00:03:21.830
- This is what they
use to make vegan eggs,

00:03:21.830 --> 00:03:23.720
it gives it more of that egg flavor

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:25.860
without adding actual egg.

00:03:25.860 --> 00:03:27.980
- You don't want it tasting
too much like farts.

00:03:27.980 --> 00:03:29.580
- Yeah, if we add too much egg,

00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:32.083
it's gonna ruin the
consistency of the ice cream.

00:03:32.294 --> 00:03:34.410
Cheers!
- Cheers!

00:03:35.590 --> 00:03:36.440
- Super egg-y.

00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:38.160
- It tastes exactly like egg tart,

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:40.760
like a creamier, eggier version of it.

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:42.640
- Only thing missing is the crust.

00:03:42.640 --> 00:03:45.700
I baked up some sticks of puff pastry,

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:48.730
so that when you scoop,
these kind of just break

00:03:49.350 --> 00:03:50.960
and you can see the flakes.

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:53.500
- Custard and then pastry.
- Exactly.

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:54.730
- Like a never ending egg tart.

00:03:54.730 --> 00:03:55.930
- Well now we're gonna go ahead

00:03:55.930 --> 00:03:58.295
and pour this mix into
the ice cream machine.

00:03:58.295 --> 00:03:59.373
- Okay, let's go.

00:03:59.373 --> 00:04:02.155
- This is a Ferrari of ice cream machines,

00:04:02.155 --> 00:04:03.655
this is the Carpigiani LV502G.

00:04:04.874 --> 00:04:06.420
Carpigiani.
- Carpigiani.

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:07.253
Lamborghini.

00:04:07.253 --> 00:04:09.860
- We pour the mix in here
and the mix gets whipped

00:04:09.860 --> 00:04:12.820
with a blade as the barrel
freezes the ice cream,

00:04:12.820 --> 00:04:16.283
creating super tight
microscopic ice crystals.

00:04:16.670 --> 00:04:17.503
- Got it.

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:24.060
Oh my god, this is some epic
egg tart waterfall right here.

00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:25.693
To the very last drop.

00:04:25.790 --> 00:04:27.520
- Put the lid on and I'm gonna have you

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:29.313
press the magic button.

00:04:29.430 --> 00:04:30.263
- Here we go.

00:04:31.530 --> 00:04:33.230
In eight minutes, we'll come back.

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:36.260
(whimsical music)

00:04:36.260 --> 00:04:37.560
- I'm gonna open the gate.

00:04:37.820 --> 00:04:42.120
- Okay, open it, oh my god!

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:44.793
This is like, what game
is this, like Tetris?

00:04:45.328 --> 00:04:48.411
(upbeat synth music)

00:04:48.558 --> 00:04:49.391
Okay, go.

00:04:50.241 --> 00:04:52.170
(upbeat music)

00:04:52.170 --> 00:04:54.063
It's not stopping, help.

00:04:54.910 --> 00:04:56.510
- Here, I'll trade you.
- Help.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:57.940
So here we are.

00:04:57.940 --> 00:04:59.490
- Almost four gallons.

00:04:59.490 --> 00:05:01.910
Just stick them in and
they're gonna get broken up.

00:05:01.910 --> 00:05:03.973
All the way down, fill that baby up.

00:05:04.050 --> 00:05:04.883
- [Inga] Yeah.

00:05:04.883 --> 00:05:06.578
- [Adrienne] And then
let's just cover them up.

00:05:06.578 --> 00:05:07.995
- [Inga] Oh yeah.

00:05:09.170 --> 00:05:11.050
- Gonna cover this with some paper

00:05:11.050 --> 00:05:12.150
and we're just gonna throw it

00:05:12.150 --> 00:05:13.893
right here in our blast freezer.

00:05:15.150 --> 00:05:18.283
We're gonna let it sit
for about 15 minutes.

00:05:18.590 --> 00:05:21.700
- We did it, first ice cream, check.

00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:23.860
- Alright, now let's do
the oolong ice cream.

00:05:23.860 --> 00:05:24.717
- Round two!

00:05:25.453 --> 00:05:28.370
(cheery whistling)

00:05:29.018 --> 00:05:29.851
- No!

00:05:32.134 --> 00:05:33.502
- [Adrienne] Open the floodgate.

00:05:33.502 --> 00:05:34.585
- Yeah, I'm scared.

00:05:34.585 --> 00:05:37.502
(cheery whistling)

00:05:39.910 --> 00:05:40.883
Okay, go, go, go, go, go!

00:05:41.919 --> 00:05:43.336
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

00:05:43.954 --> 00:05:46.073
This is giving me a panic
attack, oh my goodness.

00:05:47.987 --> 00:05:51.570
(rhythmic saxophone music)

00:05:52.879 --> 00:05:54.229
So now we keep on waiting.

00:05:54.229 --> 00:05:56.640
(clock rapidly ticking)

00:05:56.640 --> 00:06:00.520
- Alright, let's peel
back this oolong ice cream

00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:02.083
with pineapple pastry bits.

00:06:02.700 --> 00:06:05.193
- Oolong, oolong.

00:06:07.990 --> 00:06:08.883
- There you go.

00:06:09.597 --> 00:06:10.430
- Ta-da!

00:06:11.460 --> 00:06:12.713
This smells like Taiwan.

00:06:13.170 --> 00:06:16.020
But now we should do one of this

00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:17.600
and then one of the egg custard.

00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:21.433
This is the Hong Kong egg tart!

00:06:22.950 --> 00:06:25.423
Look at how the puff pastry breaks apart.

00:06:25.600 --> 00:06:29.473
I'm so excited, this is
me in ice cream form.

00:06:31.240 --> 00:06:33.373
A little bit of this,
a little bit of that.

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:37.610
I love the oolong flavor, the
creaminess of the custard,

00:06:37.610 --> 00:06:39.603
it reminds me of home, this is amazing.

00:06:40.031 --> 00:06:40.864
We did it!

00:06:41.116 --> 00:06:43.366
(cheering)

00:06:43.460 --> 00:06:45.203
So if you guys wanna eat this too,

00:06:45.350 --> 00:06:48.040
you should go to Wanderlust
Creamery right now

00:06:48.230 --> 00:06:50.400
because it's only gonna be
there for a short while.

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:52.993
I promise you, it will be worth the trip.

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:55.650
(laughing)

00:06:55.780 --> 00:06:58.530
(pleasant music)

00:07:00.170 --> 00:07:02.367
- Hey, Unsolved is on a new
channel, and now your part.

00:07:02.367 --> 00:07:03.250
Subscribe here.
- Subscribe here.

00:07:03.250 --> 00:07:04.273
That was my part.

